# Keep the deployment bundle to what the app needs at RUNTIME.
#
# legacy/ is ~11 MB of inherited code, notes and research. Most of it is the
# provenance record and belongs in the repository, but the function only needs
# the two parts the engine actually imports:
#
#   legacy/sim/              — the wrapped physics primitives. cmp_sim puts
#                              this on sys.path (see core/legacy_bridge.py),
#                              so excluding it breaks every route with
#                              ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'sim'.
#   legacy/knowledge/params/ — the inherited parameter packs that several
#                              films still resolve against.
#
# Everything else (research notes, validation trees, papers, tests) is never
# read by a request and would only slow cold starts. Verified by importing the
# app with the excluded paths removed, not by assumption — the first draft of
# this file dropped all of legacy/ and broke the import.
legacy/knowledge/cmp/
legacy/knowledge/materials/
legacy/knowledge/process/
legacy/knowledge/notes/
legacy/validation/
legacy/papers/
legacy/tests/
legacy/tools/
legacy/*.md

tests/
docs/
examples/
tools/
papers/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
